h. Let's take the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with the minimal degree "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/12f007a72f85390edd9e94ab2e722f25d10a7c825a1fc10834e8d8cec743199c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". We call the set of the vertices who are connected with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", that are not connected — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" . All vertices which don't connect with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be in the same connected component of the CG. Let's build the complemented graph to the subgraph including "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and set "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — there are "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0162135d4995e4a956e69b74a908776b8cea06924297ef1850fdc01a0d0cf99e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/31e1599aae8ab635d8d3567f239fcf6c0d10a40f00b0be012fe5d02eb4765202.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" =  "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5f8994e42d1eb800dfac0f69aa85e01f146a20101e508da6b1be0d4264e5b9dd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" =  "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") edges."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Let's build DSU for the vertices of given graph and merge components which we have found using the new-built graph. All that we should do after it is to consider vertices from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":": now we look to the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We put "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the same component as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" has edges not to all vertices of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (we do it using DSU too). The complexity of this solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mlogn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Another solution: we keep "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"set"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", which contains vertices, which haven't been visited yet. Let's run series of bfs to find the components of CG. If we are working now with the vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", pass through "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Consider "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the element of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". If edge ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") isn't in the given graph, than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is in the same component of CG as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so, we can erase it from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and add to queue. Otherwise, we do nothing."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"What is the complexity of this solution? To understand that, we must know how many times whe consider fixed vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"set"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" remains int "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" when we run to them from vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"  <  =  >  edge ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") is in the given graph. So, every vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" remains in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" no more than its degree. So, the complexity of this algorithm is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mlogn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") (log n because of binsearch — we need use it to know, is ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"u"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") in the graph). If we use "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"HashMap"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we'll get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/4556"}